IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc18-soira-notice.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 490.02 to 490.029 (the notice and obligation to
-- comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act for convictions in Canada before that Act: Form 53 notices, exemption and
-- termination orders), as isomorphic rules over the facts a person can state. Part agent ccc18; layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not
-- the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW EACH ANSWER IS READ. Every decision function answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE (the text says yes on these facts), JUST FALSE (the text
-- says no in its own words: "only if", "unless", "shall not", "may not", a period fixed in words, a condition introduced with "if"), NOTHING
-- (not covered: the text is silent, the case falls outside a limit in its own wording, or the answer points outside the text). Every branch
-- that answers no carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"`, and every branch that answers "not covered"
-- carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. A tag `[marginal (a)]` marks a branch that rests on a reading
-- left to a lawyer (NOTES.md, Marginal readings): a failed "if" counted as the text's no.
-- A judgment the text hands to a court ("if it is satisfied that the person has established ...") is an input, never computed.
-- Answers taken from other parts are inputs named `... by s <label> ...` of type MAYBE BOOLEAN (PLAN.md section 4, rule R4).
--
-- DUTIES. A duty on a named party is also a regulative rule (PARTY ... MUST ...), traced in the tests file; the duty's decision function says
-- when the duty arises. A trace prints its outcome and cannot be asserted on the stable binary (NOTES.md, What the stable binary does not accept).

§ `Sections 490.02 to 490.029 -- Notice and obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`

§ `490.02 Persons who may be served`

-- src:10275 | Persons who may be served
-- src:10276 | 490.02 (1) The Attorney General of a province or minister of justice of a territory may serve a person with a notice only if the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, an offence referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) and
-- src:10277 | (a) on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force, they are subject to a sentence for, or have not received an absolute discharge under Part XX.1 from, the offence; or
-- src:10278 | (b) in any other case,
-- src:10279 | (i) their name appears in connection with the offence, immediately before the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force, in the sex offender registry established under the Ontario Act, and
-- src:10280 | (ii) they either were a resident of Ontario at any time between April 23, 2001 and the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force or committed the offence in Ontario.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02(1) (src:10275-10280)
GIVEN `the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, an offence referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1), by s 490.011(1) designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `(a) on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force, they are subject to a sentence for, or have not received an absolute discharge under Part XX.1 from, the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b)(i) their name appears in connection with the offence, immediately before the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force, in the sex offender registry established under the Ontario Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b)(ii) they were a resident of Ontario at any time between April 23, 2001 and the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b)(ii) they committed the offence in Ontario` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02(1) the Attorney General or minister of justice may serve the person with a notice` MEANS
    IF NOT (  `(a) on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force, they are subject to a sentence for, or have not received an absolute discharge under Part XX.1 from, the offence`
           OR (  `(b)(i) their name appears in connection with the offence, immediately before the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force, in the sex offender registry established under the Ontario Act`
              AND (  `(b)(ii) they were a resident of Ontario at any time between April 23, 2001 and the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force`
                  OR `(b)(ii) they committed the offence in Ontario`)))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may serve a person with a notice only if the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, an offence referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) and"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, an offence referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1), by s 490.011(1) designated offence`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may serve a person with a notice only if the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, an offence referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d) or (e)"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) is in another part

-- src:10281 | Exception
-- src:10282 | (2) A notice shall not be served on a person
-- src:10283 | (a) if they have been finally acquitted of, or have received a free pardon granted under Her Majesty’s royal prerogative of mercy or under section 748 for, every offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act;
-- src:10284 | (b) if an application has been made for an order under subsection 490.012(3) of this Act or subsection 227.01(3) of the National Defence Act in relation to any offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act; or
-- src:10285 | (c) who is referred to in paragraph (1)(b) if they have provided proof of a pardon in accordance with subsection 9(1) of the Ontario Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02(2) (src:10281-10285)
GIVEN `(a) they have been finally acquitted of, or have received a free pardon granted under Her Majesty’s royal prerogative of mercy or under section 748 for, every offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) an application has been made for an order under subsection 490.012(3) of this Act or subsection 227.01(3) of the National Defence Act in relation to any offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) they are referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and they have provided proof of a pardon in accordance with subsection 9(1) of the Ontario Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02(2) a notice shall not be served on the person` MEANS
    IF `(a) they have been finally acquitted of, or have received a free pardon granted under Her Majesty’s royal prerogative of mercy or under section 748 for, every offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act`
       OR `(b) an application has been made for an order under subsection 490.012(3) of this Act or subsection 227.01(3) of the National Defence Act in relation to any offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act`
       OR `(c) they are referred to in paragraph (1)(b) and they have provided proof of a pardon in accordance with subsection 9(1) of the Ontario Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies: "A notice shall not be served on a person"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is limited to the cases in paragraphs (a) to (c); outside them the subsection says nothing about whether a notice may be served

-- src:10275 | Persons who may be served
-- src:10276 | 490.02 (1) The Attorney General of a province or minister of justice of a territory may serve a person with a notice only if the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, an offence referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) and
-- src:10277 | (a) on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force, they are subject to a sentence for, or have not received an absolute discharge under Part XX.1 from, the offence; or
-- src:10278 | (b) in any other case,
-- src:10279 | (i) their name appears in connection with the offence, immediately before the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force, in the sex offender registry established under the Ontario Act, and
-- src:10280 | (ii) they either were a resident of Ontario at any time between April 23, 2001 and the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force or committed the offence in Ontario.
-- src:10281 | Exception
-- src:10282 | (2) A notice shall not be served on a person
-- src:10283 | (a) if they have been finally acquitted of, or have received a free pardon granted under Her Majesty’s royal prerogative of mercy or under section 748 for, every offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act;
-- src:10284 | (b) if an application has been made for an order under subsection 490.012(3) of this Act or subsection 227.01(3) of the National Defence Act in relation to any offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act; or
-- src:10285 | (c) who is referred to in paragraph (1)(b) if they have provided proof of a pardon in accordance with subsection 9(1) of the Ontario Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02(1) and (2) (src:10275-10285)
GIVEN `the answer of s 490.02(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 490.02(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02 the notice may be served, subject to subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 490.02(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice shall not be served on a person"
    ELSE `the answer of s 490.02(1)`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("only if"); NOTHING when the offence seam is not covered

-- src:10286 | References
-- src:10287 | (3) The reference in subsection (1) to the definition designated offence is a reference to that definition as it read from time to time before the day on which this subsection comes into force, and the reference in paragraph (2)(b) to subsection 490.012(3) is a reference to that provision as it read from time to time before that day.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02(3) (src:10286-10287)
DECLARE `s 490.02(3) reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.02(3) the reference in subsection (1) to the definition designated offence`
    `s 490.02(3) the reference in paragraph (2)(b) to subsection 490.012(3)`
    `s 490.02(3) any other reference`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02(3) (src:10286-10287)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 490.02(3) reference`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02(3) the reference is to the provision as it read from time to time before the day on which the subsection comes into force` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `s 490.02(3) the reference in subsection (1) to the definition designated offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02(3) the reference in paragraph (2)(b) to subsection 490.012(3)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02(3) any other reference` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two references and says nothing of any other

§ `490.021 Period for and method of service`

-- src:10288 | Period for and method of service
-- src:10289 | 490.021 (1) The notice shall be personally served within one year after the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(1) (src:10288-10289)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 490.021(1) one year after the day` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d PLUS 1)   -- the same date a year later (a 29 February rolls to 1 March: NOTES.md, fork F3)

@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(1) (src:10288-10289)
GIVEN `the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the notice is served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.021(1) the notice is served within one year after the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the notice is served` GREATER THAN `the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force`
       AND `the day on which the notice is served` AT MOST `s 490.021(1) one year after the day` `the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice shall be personally served within one year after the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force"

-- src:10290 | Exception
-- src:10291 | (2) If a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(a) is unlawfully at large or is in breach of any terms of their sentence or discharge, or of any conditions set under this Act or under Part III of the National Defence Act, that relate to residence, the notice may be served by registered mail at their last known address.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(2) (src:10290-10291)
GIVEN `the person is referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is unlawfully at large` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in breach of any terms of their sentence or discharge, or of any conditions set under this Act or under Part III of the National Defence Act, that relate to residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.021(2) the notice may be served by registered mail at the person's last known address` MEANS
    IF `the person is referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(a)`
       AND (`the person is unlawfully at large` OR `the person is in breach of any terms of their sentence or discharge, or of any conditions set under this Act or under Part III of the National Defence Act, that relate to residence`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is given "If a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(a) is unlawfully at large or is in breach"; outside that case the subsection grants nothing

-- src:10292 | Exception
-- src:10293 | (3) If a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) is not in compliance with section 3 of the Ontario Act on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force, the notice may be served by registered mail at their last known address.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(3) (src:10292-10293)
GIVEN `the person is referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not in compliance with section 3 of the Ontario Act on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.021(3) the notice may be served by registered mail at the person's last known address, the person not being in compliance with the Ontario Act` MEANS
    IF `the person is referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b)` AND `the person is not in compliance with section 3 of the Ontario Act on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is given "If a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) is not in compliance with section 3 of the Ontario Act"

-- src:10294 | Exception
-- src:10295 | (4) If a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) is in compliance with section 3 and subsection 7(2) of the Ontario Act on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force but fails to comply with subsection 3(1) or 7(2) of the Ontario Act within one year after that day, the notice shall be served within one year after the day on which they failed to comply and may be served by registered mail at their last known address.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(4) (src:10294-10295)
GIVEN `the person is referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in compliance with section 3 and subsection 7(2) of the Ontario Act on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with subsection 3(1) or 7(2) of the Ontario Act within one year after that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.021(4) the notice may be served by registered mail at the person's last known address, the person having failed to comply` MEANS
    IF `the person is referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b)`
       AND `the person is in compliance with section 3 and subsection 7(2) of the Ontario Act on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force`
       AND `the person fails to comply with subsection 3(1) or 7(2) of the Ontario Act within one year after that day`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is given "If a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) is in compliance with section 3 and subsection 7(2) of the Ontario Act"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(4) (src:10294-10295)
GIVEN `the day on which the person failed to comply` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the notice is served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.021(4) the notice is served within one year after the day on which the person failed to comply` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the notice is served` GREATER THAN `the day on which the person failed to comply`
       AND `the day on which the notice is served` AT MOST `s 490.021(1) one year after the day` `the day on which the person failed to comply`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice shall be served within one year after the day on which they failed to comply"

-- src:10288 | Period for and method of service
-- src:10289 | 490.021 (1) The notice shall be personally served within one year after the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force.
-- src:10290 | Exception
-- src:10291 | (2) If a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(a) is unlawfully at large or is in breach of any terms of their sentence or discharge, or of any conditions set under this Act or under Part III of the National Defence Act, that relate to residence, the notice may be served by registered mail at their last known address.
-- src:10292 | Exception
-- src:10293 | (3) If a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) is not in compliance with section 3 of the Ontario Act on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force, the notice may be served by registered mail at their last known address.
-- src:10294 | Exception
-- src:10295 | (4) If a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) is in compliance with section 3 and subsection 7(2) of the Ontario Act on the day on which the Sex Offender Information Registration Act comes into force but fails to comply with subsection 3(1) or 7(2) of the Ontario Act within one year after that day, the notice shall be served within one year after the day on which they failed to comply and may be served by registered mail at their last known address.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(1) to (4) (src:10288-10295)
DECLARE `s 490.021(1) manner of service` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.021(1) personal service`
    `s 490.021(2) registered mail at the last known address`
    `s 490.021(1) another manner of service`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(1) to (4) (src:10288-10295)
GIVEN manner IS A `s 490.021(1) manner of service`
      `the answer of s 490.021(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 490.021(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 490.021(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.021 the manner of service is one the section allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER manner
    WHEN `s 490.021(1) personal service` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.021(2) registered mail at the last known address` THEN
        IF `the answer of s 490.021(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of s 490.021(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of s 490.021(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice shall be personally served" (registered mail is allowed only in the cases of subsections (2), (3) and (4))
    WHEN `s 490.021(1) another manner of service` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice shall be personally served"

-- src:10296 | Proof of service
-- src:10297 | (5) An affidavit of the person who served the notice, sworn before a commissioner or other person authorized to take affidavits, is evidence of the service and the notice if it sets out that
-- src:10298 | (a) the person who served the notice has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case;
-- src:10299 | (b) the notice was personally served on, or mailed to, the person to whom it was directed on a named day; and
-- src:10300 | (c) the person who served the notice identifies a true copy of the notice as an exhibit attached to the affidavit.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(5) (src:10296-10300)
GIVEN `it is an affidavit of the person who served the notice, sworn before a commissioner or other person authorized to take affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) it sets out that the person who served the notice has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) it sets out that the notice was personally served on, or mailed to, the person to whom it was directed on a named day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) it sets out that the person who served the notice identifies a true copy of the notice as an exhibit attached to the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.021(5) the affidavit is evidence of the service and the notice` MEANS
    IF `it is an affidavit of the person who served the notice, sworn before a commissioner or other person authorized to take affidavits`
       AND `(a) it sets out that the person who served the notice has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case`
       AND `(b) it sets out that the notice was personally served on, or mailed to, the person to whom it was directed on a named day`
       AND `(c) it sets out that the person who served the notice identifies a true copy of the notice as an exhibit attached to the affidavit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is evidence of the service and the notice if it sets out that" [marginal (a)]

-- src:10301 | Requirements relating to notice
-- src:10302 | (6) The person who served the notice shall, without delay, send a copy of the affidavit and the notice to the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the person was served.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(6) (src:10301-10302)
DECLARE `s 490.021(6) party` IS ONE OF `s 490.021(6) the person who served the notice`   -- not in the core's Party: NEEDS-CORE.md
DECLARE `s 490.021(6) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.021(6) send a copy of the affidavit and the notice to the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the person was served`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(6) (src:10301-10302)
GIVEN `they served the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.021(6) the person who served the notice must send a copy of the affidavit and the notice` MEANS
    IF `they served the notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid on "The person who served the notice"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.021(6) (src:10301-10302)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 490.021(6) party` `s 490.021(6) action`
`s 490.021(6) the duty of the person who served the notice, without delay` MEANS
    PARTY `s 490.021(6) the person who served the notice`
    MUST `s 490.021(6) send a copy of the affidavit and the notice to the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the person was served`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 490.021(6) the person who served the notice` BECAUSE "the copy of the affidavit and the notice was not sent to the Attorney General or minister of justice"

§ `490.022 Date obligation begins; date obligation ends; duration of obligation`

-- src:10303 | Date obligation begins
-- src:10304 | 490.022 (1) The obligation under section 490.019 begins
-- src:10305 | (a) either one year after the day on which the person is served with the notice or when an exemption order is refused under subsection 490.023(2), whichever is later; or
-- src:10306 | (b) when an exemption order is quashed.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.022(1) (src:10303-10306)
GIVEN `the day on which the person is served with the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day on which an exemption order is refused under subsection 490.023(2), if it is` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which an exemption order is quashed, if it is` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 490.022(1) the day on which the obligation under section 490.019 begins` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which an exemption order is quashed, if it is`
    WHEN JUST quashed THEN quashed   -- (b) when an exemption order is quashed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN                -- (a) either one year after the day on which the person is served or when an exemption order is refused, whichever is later
        CONSIDER `the day on which an exemption order is refused under subsection 490.023(2), if it is`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 490.021(1) one year after the day` `the day on which the person is served with the notice`
        WHEN JUST refused THEN
            IF refused AT LEAST `s 490.021(1) one year after the day` `the day on which the person is served with the notice`
            THEN refused
            ELSE `s 490.021(1) one year after the day` `the day on which the person is served with the notice`

-- src:10307 | Date obligation ends
-- src:10308 | (2) The obligation ends on the earliest of
-- src:10309 | (a) the day on which an exemption order is made on an appeal from a decision made under subsection 490.023(2),
-- src:10310 | (b) the day on which the obligation of a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) to comply with section 3 of the Ontario Act ends under paragraph 7(1)(a) of that Act, or
-- src:10311 | (c) the day on which a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) provides satisfactory proof of a pardon or record suspension to a person who collects information, as defined in subsection 3(1) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, at a registration centre.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.022(2) (src:10307-10311)
GIVEN `(a) the day on which an exemption order is made on an appeal from a decision made under subsection 490.023(2), if it is` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `(b) the day on which the obligation of a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) to comply with section 3 of the Ontario Act ends under paragraph 7(1)(a) of that Act, if it does` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `(c) the day on which a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) provides satisfactory proof of a pardon or record suspension to a person who collects information at a registration centre, if they do` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 490.022(2) the earliest day on which the obligation ends` MEANS
    `earlier` (`earlier` `(a) the day on which an exemption order is made on an appeal from a decision made under subsection 490.023(2), if it is` `(b) the day on which the obligation of a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) to comply with section 3 of the Ontario Act ends under paragraph 7(1)(a) of that Act, if it does`) `(c) the day on which a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) provides satisfactory proof of a pardon or record suspension to a person who collects information at a registration centre, if they do`
    WHERE
        `earlier` x y MEANS
            CONSIDER x
            WHEN NOTHING THEN y   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): when none of paragraphs (a) to (c) occurs, subsection (3) governs, and this subsection gives no day
            WHEN JUST a THEN
                CONSIDER y
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST a
                WHEN JUST b THEN IF a AT MOST b THEN JUST a ELSE JUST b

-- src:10312 | Duration of obligation
-- src:10313 | (3) If none of paragraphs (2)(a) to (c) applies earlier, the obligation
-- src:10314 | (a) ends 10 years after the person was sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice if the offence was prosecuted summarily or if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is two or five years;
-- src:10315 | (b) ends 20 years after the person was sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is 10 or 14 years;
-- src:10316 | (c) applies for life if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence listed in the notice is life; or
-- src:10317 | (d) applies for life if, at any time, the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, more than one offence that is referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) of this Act or in paragraph (a) or (c) of the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act and if more than one of those offences is listed in the notice.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.022(3) (src:10312-10317)
DECLARE `s 490.022(3) maximum term band` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of two or five years`
    `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of 10 or 14 years`
    `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of life`
    `s 490.022(3) any other maximum term, or none stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.022(3) (src:10312-10317)
GIVEN term IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A `s 490.022(3) maximum term band`
`s 490.022(3) the band of the maximum term of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of life`
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` t THEN
        IF t's months EQUALS 0 AND t's days EQUALS 0 AND (NOT t's `less a day`)
        THEN BRANCH IF t's years EQUALS 2 THEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of two or five years`
                    IF t's years EQUALS 5 THEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of two or five years`
                    IF t's years EQUALS 10 THEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of 10 or 14 years`
                    IF t's years EQUALS 14 THEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of 10 or 14 years`
                    OTHERWISE `s 490.022(3) any other maximum term, or none stated`
        ELSE `s 490.022(3) any other maximum term, or none stated`
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN `s 490.022(3) any other maximum term, or none stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.022(3) (src:10312-10317)
DECLARE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.022(3) ends on` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `s 490.022(3) applies for life`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.022(3) (src:10312-10317)
GIVEN d IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d PLUS n)

@ref Criminal Code s 490.022(3) (src:10312-10317)
GIVEN `the offence listed in the notice was prosecuted summarily` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence listed in the notice` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the day on which the person was sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice` IS A DATE
      `(d) at any time the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, more than one offence referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) of this Act or in paragraph (a) or (c) of the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(d) more than one of those offences is listed in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation`
`s 490.022(3) the obligation, if none of paragraphs (2)(a) to (c) applies earlier, ends or applies for life` MEANS
    IF `(d) at any time the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, more than one offence referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) of this Act or in paragraph (a) or (c) of the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act`
       AND `(d) more than one of those offences is listed in the notice`
    THEN JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life`   -- paragraph (d)
    ELSE IF `the offence listed in the notice was prosecuted summarily` OR `s 490.022(3) the band of the maximum term of imprisonment` `the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence listed in the notice` EQUALS `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of two or five years`
         THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (`s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the person was sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice` 10))   -- paragraph (a): 10 years
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 490.022(3) the band of the maximum term of imprisonment` `the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence listed in the notice`
              WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of 10 or 14 years` THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (`s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the person was sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice` 20))   -- paragraph (b): 20 years
              WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of life` THEN JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life`   -- paragraph (c)
              WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of two or five years` THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (`s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the person was sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice` 10))
              WHEN `s 490.022(3) any other maximum term, or none stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names maximum terms of two, five, 10, 14 years and life only

-- src:10318 | Reference
-- src:10319 | (4) The reference in paragraph (3)(d) to the definition designated offence is to a reference to that definition as it read from time to time before the day on which this subsection comes into force.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.022(4) (src:10318-10319)
DECLARE `s 490.022(4) reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.022(4) the reference in paragraph (3)(d) to the definition designated offence`
    `s 490.022(4) any other reference`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.022(4) (src:10318-10319)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 490.022(4) reference`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.022(4) the reference is to the definition as it read from time to time before the day on which the subsection comes into force` MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `s 490.022(4) the reference in paragraph (3)(d) to the definition designated offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.022(4) any other reference` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of the reference in paragraph (3)(d)

§ `490.023 Application for exemption order`

-- src:10320 | Application for exemption order
-- src:10321 | 490.023 (1) A person who is not subject to an order under section 490.012 of this Act or section 227.01 of the National Defence Act may apply for an order exempting them from the obligation within one year after they are served with a notice under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(1) (src:10320-10321)
GIVEN `s 490.012 an order to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act is in force` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN   -- the person is subject to "an order under section 490.012 of this Act or section 227.01 of the National Defence Act"
      `the day on which they were served with a notice under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply for an order exempting them from the obligation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.023(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` MEANS
    IF `the day on which they apply for an order exempting them from the obligation` LESS THAN `the day on which they were served with a notice under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act`
       OR `the day on which they apply for an order exempting them from the obligation` GREATER THAN `s 490.021(1) one year after the day` `the day on which they were served with a notice under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply for an order exempting them from the obligation within one year after they are served with a notice"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 490.012 an order to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act is in force`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is not subject to an order under section 490.012 of this Act or section 227.01 of the National Defence Act may apply"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an order under section 490.012 is in force is answered by another part

-- src:10322 | Jurisdiction
-- src:10323 | (1.1) The application shall be made to a court of criminal jurisdiction if
-- src:10324 | (a) it relates to an obligation under section 490.019 of this Act; or
-- src:10325 | (b) it relates to an obligation under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act and the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.1(2) of that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(1.1) (src:10322-10325)
GIVEN `(a) the application relates to an obligation under section 490.019 of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the application relates to an obligation under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.1(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.023(1.1) the application shall be made to a court of criminal jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `(a) the application relates to an obligation under section 490.019 of this Act`
       OR (`(b) the application relates to an obligation under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act` AND `(b) the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.1(2) of that Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application shall be made to a court of criminal jurisdiction if" [marginal (a)]

-- src:10326 | Exemption order
-- src:10327 | (2) The court shall make an exemption order if it is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of the obligation on them, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(2) (src:10326-10327)
DECLARE `s 490.023(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.023(2) make an exemption order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(2) (src:10326-10327)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of the obligation on them, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.023(2) the court shall make an exemption order` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of the obligation on them, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall make an exemption order if it is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of the obligation on them" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(2) (src:10326-10327)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.023(2) action`
`s 490.023(2) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.023(2) make an exemption order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of the grounds and did not make an exemption order"

-- src:10328 | Reasons for decision
-- src:10329 | (3) The court shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(3) (src:10328-10329)
DECLARE `s 490.023(3) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.023(3) give reasons for its decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(3) (src:10328-10329)
GIVEN `the court has made a decision under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.023(3) the court shall give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a decision under subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "The court shall give reasons for its decision"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(3) (src:10328-10329)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.023(3) action`
`s 490.023(3) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.023(3) give reasons for its decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not give reasons for its decision"

-- src:10330 | Removal of information from database
-- src:10331 | (4) If the court makes an exemption order, it shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of the copy of the notice.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(4) (src:10330-10331)
DECLARE `s 490.023(4) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.023(4) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of the copy of the notice`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(4) (src:10330-10331)
GIVEN `the court makes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.023(4) the court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an exemption order` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court makes an exemption order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.023(4) (src:10330-10331)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.023(4) action`
`s 490.023(4) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.023(4) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of the copy of the notice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
