§ `490.024 Appeal`

-- src:10332 | Appeal
-- src:10333 | 490.024 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order may appeal from a decision of the court under subsection 490.023(2) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may dismiss the appeal, or allow it and order a new hearing, quash the exemption order or make an order that may be made under that subsection.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.024(1) (src:10332-10333)
DECLARE `s 490.024(1) appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.024(1) the Attorney General`
    `s 490.024(1) the person who applied for an exemption order`
    `s 490.024(1) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.024(1) (src:10332-10333)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 490.024(1) appellant`
      `the decision appealed from is a decision of the court under subsection 490.023(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.024(1) the appeal may be brought` MEANS
    IF appellant EQUALS `s 490.024(1) another person` OR (NOT `the decision appealed from is a decision of the court under subsection 490.023(2)`) OR (NOT `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order may appeal from a decision of the court under subsection 490.023(2) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10333 | 490.024 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order may appeal from a decision of the court under subsection 490.023(2) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may dismiss the appeal, or allow it and order a new hearing, quash the exemption order or make an order that may be made under that subsection.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.024(1) (src:10333-10333)
DECLARE `s 490.024(1) thing the appeal court does` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.024(1) dismiss the appeal`
    `s 490.024(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing`
    `s 490.024(1) quash the exemption order`
    `s 490.024(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.023(2)`
    `s 490.024(1) another thing`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.024(1) (src:10333-10333)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 490.024(1) thing the appeal court does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.024(1) the appeal court may do it` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 490.024(1) dismiss the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.024(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.024(1) quash the exemption order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.024(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.023(2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.024(1) another thing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The appeal court may dismiss the appeal, or allow it and order a new hearing, quash the exemption order or make an order that may be made under that subsection"

-- src:10334 | Removal of information from database
-- src:10335 | (2) If the appeal court makes an exemption order, it shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of the copy of the notice.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.024(2) (src:10334-10335)
DECLARE `s 490.024(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.024(2) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of the copy of the notice`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.024(2) (src:10334-10335)
