§ `490.025 Requirements relating to notice`

-- src:10336 | Requirements relating to notice
-- src:10337 | 490.025 If a court refuses to make an exemption order or an appeal court dismisses an appeal from such a decision or quashes an exemption order, it shall cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision and shall cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.025 (src:10336-10337)
GIVEN `a court refuses to make an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal court dismisses an appeal from such a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal court quashes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.025 the court shall cause the notification and the information to be given` MEANS
    IF `a court refuses to make an exemption order` OR `an appeal court dismisses an appeal from such a decision` OR `an appeal court quashes an exemption order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a court refuses to make an exemption order or an appeal court dismisses an appeal from such a decision or quashes an exemption order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.025 (src:10336-10337)
DECLARE `s 490.025 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.025 cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision`
    `s 490.025 cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.025 (src:10336-10337)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.025 action`
`s 490.025 the duty of the court to cause the Commissioner and the Attorney General to be notified` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.025 cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the Commissioner and the Attorney General were not notified of the decision"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.025 (src:10336-10337)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.025 action`
`s 490.025 the duty of the court to cause the person to be informed of the sections` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.025 cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the person who applied was not informed of the sections"

§ `490.026 Application for termination order`

-- src:10338 | Application for termination order
-- src:10339 | 490.026 (1) A person who is subject to an obligation under section 490.019 may apply for a termination order unless they are also subject to an obligation under section 490.02901, under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act — or an order under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act — that began later.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.026(1) (src:10338-10339)
GIVEN `s 490.019 the person is subject to an obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `they are also subject to an obligation under section 490.02901, under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, or to an order under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act, that began later` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.026(1) the person may apply for a termination order` MEANS
    IF `they are also subject to an obligation under section 490.02901, under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, or to an order under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act, that began later`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply for a termination order unless they are also subject to an obligation under section 490.02901"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 490.019 the person is subject to an obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is subject to an obligation under section 490.019 may apply"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is subject to an obligation under section 490.019 is answered by another part

-- src:10340 | Time for application
-- src:10341 | (2) A person may apply for a termination order if the following period has elapsed since they were sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice:
-- src:10342 | (a) five years if the offence was prosecuted summarily or if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is two or five years;
-- src:10343 | (b) 10 years if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is 10 or 14 years; or
-- src:10344 | (c) 20 years if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is life.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.026(2) (src:10340-10344)
GIVEN `the offence listed in the notice was prosecuted summarily` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence listed in the notice` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the day on which they were sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply for a termination order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.026(2) the person may apply for a termination order, the period since sentence having elapsed` MEANS
    IF `the offence listed in the notice was prosecuted summarily` THEN `the period of` 5   -- (a) five years if the offence was prosecuted summarily
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 490.022(3) the band of the maximum term of imprisonment` `the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence listed in the notice`
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of two or five years` THEN `the period of` 5   -- (a) five years if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is two or five years
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of 10 or 14 years` THEN `the period of` 10   -- (b)
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of life` THEN `the period of` 20   -- (c)
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) any other maximum term, or none stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names maximum terms of two, five, 10, 14 years and life only
    WHERE
        `the period of` n MEANS
            IF `the day on which they apply for a termination order` AT LEAST `s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which they were sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice` n
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person may apply for a termination order if the following period has elapsed" (fork F5: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:10345 | More than one offence
-- src:10346 | (3) If more than one offence is listed in the notice, the person may apply for a termination order if 20 years have elapsed since they were sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the most recent offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.026(3) (src:10345-10346)
GIVEN `more than one offence is listed in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which they were sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the most recent offence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply for a termination order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.026(3) the person may apply for a termination order, 20 years having elapsed since the most recent offence` MEANS
    IF `more than one offence is listed in the notice`
       AND `the day on which they apply for a termination order` AT LEAST `s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which they were sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the most recent offence` 20
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If more than one offence is listed in the notice, the person may apply for a termination order if 20 years have elapsed" (fork F5: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:10347 | Pardon, record suspension or absolute discharge
-- src:10348 | (4) Despite subsections (2) and (3), a person may apply for a termination order once they receive a pardon, once a record suspension is ordered or once they are absolutely discharged under paragraph 672.54(a).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.026(4) (src:10347-10348)
GIVEN `they receive a pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a record suspension is ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are absolutely discharged under paragraph 672.54(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.026(4) the person may apply for a termination order, despite subsections (2) and (3)` MEANS
    IF `they receive a pardon` OR `a record suspension is ordered` OR `they are absolutely discharged under paragraph 672.54(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person may apply for a termination order once they receive a pardon, once a record suspension is ordered or once they are absolutely discharged under paragraph 672.54(a)" [may-where] ("once" read as "when": ruling (b) of the periods ruling; name-test sweep of 2026-11-12)

-- src:10349 | Re-application
-- src:10350 | (5) A person whose application is refused may apply again if five years have elapsed since they made the previous application. They may also apply again once they receive a pardon or once a record suspension is ordered. However, they may not apply again if, after the previous application was made, they become subject to an obligation under section 490.02901, under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act or to an order under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.026(5) (src:10349-10350)
GIVEN `their application was refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which they made the previous application` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply again` IS A DATE
      `they receive a pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a record suspension is ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after the previous application was made, they become subject to an obligation under section 490.02901, under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act or to an order under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.026(5) the person may apply again for a termination order` MEANS
    IF NOT `their application was refused`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person whose application is refused may apply again"
    ELSE IF `after the previous application was made, they become subject to an obligation under section 490.02901, under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act or under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act or to an order under section 490.012 or under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they may not apply again if, after the previous application was made, they become subject to an obligation under section 490.02901"
         ELSE IF `the day on which they apply again` AT LEAST `s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which they made the previous application` 5 OR `they receive a pardon` OR `a record suspension is ordered`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may apply again if five years have elapsed since they made the previous application" or "once they receive a pardon or once a record suspension is ordered" (fork F5)

-- src:10351 | Jurisdiction
-- src:10352 | (6) The application shall be made to a court of criminal jurisdiction if
-- src:10353 | (a) it relates to an obligation under section 490.019 of this Act; or
-- src:10354 | (b) it relates to an obligation under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act and the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.12(6) of that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.026(6) (src:10351-10354)
GIVEN `(a) the application relates to an obligation under section 490.019 of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the application relates to an obligation under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.12(6) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.026(6) the application shall be made to a court of criminal jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `(a) the application relates to an obligation under section 490.019 of this Act`
       OR (`(b) the application relates to an obligation under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act` AND `(b) the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.12(6) of that Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application shall be made to a court of criminal jurisdiction if" [marginal (a)]

§ `490.027 Termination order`

-- src:10355 | Termination order
-- src:10356 | 490.027 (1) The court shall make an order terminating the obligation if it is satisfied that the person has established that
-- src:10357 | (a) there would be no connection between continuing the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act; or
-- src:10358 | (b) the impact on the person of continuing the obligation, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(1) (src:10355-10358)
DECLARE `s 490.027(1) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.027(1) make an order terminating the obligation`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(1) (src:10355-10358)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the person has established that there would be no connection between continuing the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact on the person of continuing the obligation, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.027(1) the court shall make an order terminating the obligation` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that there would be no connection between continuing the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
       OR `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact on the person of continuing the obligation, including on their privacy or liberty, would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall make an order terminating the obligation if it is satisfied that the person has established that" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(1) (src:10355-10358)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.027(1) action`
`s 490.027(1) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.027(1) make an order terminating the obligation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of a ground and did not make an order terminating the obligation"

-- src:10359 | Factors
-- src:10360 | (1.1) In determining whether to make the termination order, the court shall consider
-- src:10361 | (a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation;
-- src:10362 | (b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics;
-- src:10363 | (c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim;
-- src:10364 | (d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person;
-- src:10365 | (e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence;
-- src:10366 | (f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person; and
-- src:10367 | (g) any other factors that the court considers relevant.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(1.1) (src:10359-10367)
DECLARE `s 490.027(1.1) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.027(1.1)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation`
    `s 490.027(1.1)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics`
    `s 490.027(1.1)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim`
    `s 490.027(1.1)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person`
    `s 490.027(1.1)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence`
    `s 490.027(1.1)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person`
    `s 490.027(1.1)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant`
    `s 490.027(1.1) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(1.1) (src:10359-10367)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether to make the termination order` IS A BOOLEAN
      factor IS A `s 490.027(1.1) factor`
      `the court considers the matter relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.027(1.1) the court shall consider the factor` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is determining whether to make the termination order`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In determining whether to make the termination order, the court shall consider" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE CONSIDER factor
         WHEN `s 490.027(1.1)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.027(1.1)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.027(1.1)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.027(1.1)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.027(1.1)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.027(1.1)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.027(1.1)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (g): "any other factors that the court considers relevant" is itself in the list
         WHEN `s 490.027(1.1) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` THEN IF `the court considers the matter relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only factors "that the court considers relevant" are added by paragraph (g)

-- src:10368 | Reasons for decision
-- src:10369 | (2) The court shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(2) (src:10368-10369)
DECLARE `s 490.027(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.027(2) give reasons for its decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(2) (src:10368-10369)
GIVEN `the court has made a decision under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.027(2) the court shall give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a decision under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "The court shall give reasons for its decision"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(2) (src:10368-10369)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.027(2) action`
`s 490.027(2) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.027(2) give reasons for its decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not give reasons for its decision"

-- src:10370 | Requirements relating to notice
-- src:10371 | (3) If the court makes a termination order, it shall cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, to be notified of the decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(3) (src:10370-10371)
DECLARE `s 490.027(3) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.027(3) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, to be notified of the decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(3) (src:10370-10371)
GIVEN `the court makes a termination order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.027(3) the court shall cause the notification to be given` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a termination order` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court makes a termination order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.027(3) (src:10370-10371)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.027(3) action`
`s 490.027(3) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.027(3) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, to be notified of the decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made a termination order and did not cause the notification to be given"

§ `490.028 Deemed application`

-- src:10372 | Deemed application
-- src:10373 | 490.028 If a person is eligible to apply for both an exemption order under section 490.023 and a termination order under section 490.026 within one year after they are served with a notice under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act, an application within that period for one order is deemed to be an application for both.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.028 (src:10372-10373)
GIVEN `a person is eligible to apply for both an exemption order under section 490.023 and a termination order under section 490.026 within one year after they are served with a notice under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application within that period for one order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.028 an application for one order is deemed to be an application for both` MEANS
    IF `a person is eligible to apply for both an exemption order under section 490.023 and a termination order under section 490.026 within one year after they are served with a notice under section 490.021 of this Act or section 227.08 of the National Defence Act`
       AND `an application within that period for one order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person is eligible to apply for both an exemption order under section 490.023 and a termination order under section 490.026 within one year" [marginal (a)]

§ `490.029 Appeal`

-- src:10374 | Appeal
-- src:10375 | 490.029 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for a termination order may appeal from a decision of the court made under subsection 490.027(1) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may dismiss the appeal, or allow it and order a new hearing, quash the termination order or make an order that may be made under that subsection.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029(1) (src:10374-10375)
DECLARE `s 490.029(1) appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.029(1) the Attorney General`
    `s 490.029(1) the person who applied for a termination order`
    `s 490.029(1) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029(1) (src:10374-10375)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 490.029(1) appellant`
      `the decision appealed from is a decision of the court made under subsection 490.027(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029(1) the appeal may be brought` MEANS
    IF appellant EQUALS `s 490.029(1) another person` OR (NOT `the decision appealed from is a decision of the court made under subsection 490.027(1)`) OR (NOT `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General or the person who applied for a termination order may appeal from a decision of the court made under subsection 490.027(1) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10375 | 490.029 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for a termination order may appeal from a decision of the court made under subsection 490.027(1) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may dismiss the appeal, or allow it and order a new hearing, quash the termination order or make an order that may be made under that subsection.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029(1) (src:10375-10375)
DECLARE `s 490.029(1) thing the appeal court does` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.029(1) dismiss the appeal`
    `s 490.029(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing`
    `s 490.029(1) quash the termination order`
    `s 490.029(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.027(1)`
    `s 490.029(1) another thing`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029(1) (src:10375-10375)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 490.029(1) thing the appeal court does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029(1) the appeal court may do it` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 490.029(1) dismiss the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.029(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.029(1) quash the termination order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.029(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.027(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.029(1) another thing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The appeal court may dismiss the appeal, or allow it and order a new hearing, quash the termination order or make an order that may be made under that subsection"

-- src:10376 | Requirements relating to notice
-- src:10377 | (2) If the appeal court makes an order that may be made under subsection 490.027(1), it shall cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029(2) (src:10376-10377)
DECLARE `s 490.029(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.029(2) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029(2) (src:10376-10377)
GIVEN `the appeal court makes an order that may be made under subsection 490.027(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` MEANS
    IF `the appeal court makes an order that may be made under subsection 490.027(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the appeal court makes an order that may be made under subsection 490.027(1)" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029(2) (src:10376-10377)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.029(2) action`
`s 490.029(2) the duty of a court of appeal` MEANS
    PARTY `a court of appeal`
    MUST `s 490.029(2) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a court of appeal` BECAUSE "the appeal court made an order and did not cause the notification to be given"

-- src:10307 | Date obligation ends
-- src:10308 | (2) The obligation ends on the earliest of
-- src:10309 | (a) the day on which an exemption order is made on an appeal from a decision made under subsection 490.023(2),
-- src:10310 | (b) the day on which the obligation of a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) to comply with section 3 of the Ontario Act ends under paragraph 7(1)(a) of that Act, or
-- src:10311 | (c) the day on which a person referred to in paragraph 490.02(1)(b) provides satisfactory proof of a pardon or record suspension to a person who collects information, as defined in subsection 3(1) of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, at a registration centre.
-- src:10312 | Duration of obligation
-- src:10313 | (3) If none of paragraphs (2)(a) to (c) applies earlier, the obligation
-- src:10314 | (a) ends 10 years after the person was sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice if the offence was prosecuted summarily or if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is two or five years;
-- src:10315 | (b) ends 20 years after the person was sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for the offence listed in the notice if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence is 10 or 14 years;
-- src:10316 | (c) applies for life if the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence listed in the notice is life; or
-- src:10317 | (d) applies for life if, at any time, the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, more than one offence that is referred to in paragraph (a), (c), (c.1), (d) or (e) of the definition designated offence in subsection 490.011(1) of this Act or in paragraph (a) or (c) of the definition designated offence in section 227 of the National Defence Act and if more than one of those offences is listed in the notice.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.022(2) and (3) (src:10307-10317)
GIVEN `the answer of s 490.022(2)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the answer of s 490.022(3)` IS A MAYBE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation`
`s 490.022 the obligation ends, or applies for life` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 490.022(2)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the answer of s 490.022(3)`   -- no day of subsection (2) occurs: subsection (3) governs
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        CONSIDER `the answer of s 490.022(3)`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` d)   -- subsection (2) ends it whatever subsection (3) says
        WHEN JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life` THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` d)   -- "If none of paragraphs (2)(a) to (c) applies earlier": a day of subsection (2) comes before a life-long obligation ends
        WHEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` e) THEN IF d AT MOST e THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` d) ELSE JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` e)   -- the earliest
